diff --git a/Packages/MarkdownView/README.md b/Packages/MarkdownView/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e9d726b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Packages/MarkdownView/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+# MarkdownView
+
+The assistant's Markdown renderer, vendored from source so the app can ship
+on iOS 15.
+
+[Lakr233/MarkdownView](https://github.com/Lakr233/MarkdownView) declares
+`.iOS(.v16)` in every release it has published, and SwiftPM refuses to
+resolve a package whose floor is above the one asking for it — so no version
+of the dependency can be named from a project that targets 15. Its code,
+however, only needs 16 in the places listed below, all of which are either
+guarded already or in targets this app does not build. Vendoring it is
+therefore a change of declaration, not a port.
+
+| Directory | What it is | Origin | License |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `Sources/MarkdownView` | The renderer: text view, streaming, tables, code, math | [Lakr233/MarkdownView](https://github.com/Lakr233/MarkdownView) 4.8.5 (`3941f185`, the revision the app had pinned) | MIT (`LICENSE`) |
+| `Sources/MarkdownParser` | The parser product | same | MIT (`LICENSE`) |
+| `Sources/WatchMarkdownView` | The watchOS target; not built by this app | same | MIT (`LICENSE`) |
+| `Tests` | The package's own tests; not run by `make harness` | same | MIT (`LICENSE`) |
+
+## What changed from 4.8.5
+
+1. `Package.swift`: `.iOS(.v16)` → `.iOS(.v15)`, `.macCatalyst(.v16)` →
+   `.macCatalyst(.v15)`. `macOS(.v13)` stays, which is what the package's
+   own tests need to build on the machine that runs them. `watchOS(.v8)`
+   stays.
+2. `Package.swift`: the `MarkdownViewCatalog` and `MarkdownViewBenchmark`
+   executable targets are gone, with their sources. They are the only code
+   in the package that needs iOS 16 — `Task.sleep(for:)`, `Duration`,
+   `ContinuousClock` and `.scrollContentBackground` — and they are demo
+   apps, not part of the renderer; leaving them in would make the package
+   claim an iOS 15 floor it cannot keep. Restore them from upstream if you
+   ever need to run the catalogue on a Mac.
+
+Nothing else differs: the rest of the tree is 4.8.5 verbatim.
+
+## The iOS 16 code that stays
+
+- `Components/TableView/TableView+Selection.swift`: `TextSelectionGroupDelegate`'s
+  edit-menu method, under `@available(iOS 16.0, macCatalyst 16.0, visionOS 1.0, *)`.
+- `Components/TableView/TableRowLimit.swift`: an iOS 17 SF Symbol inside
+  `if #available(iOS 17, …)`, with an older symbol in the `else`.
+- `Components/TableView/TableView+Selection.swift` and the rest of
+  `Sources/MarkdownView`: no other 16-only API. The only sleep in the
+  library is `Task.sleep(nanoseconds:)` in `MarkdownView+Coordinator.swift`,
+  which is iOS 13.
+
+Dependencies are unchanged and all inside the app's floor: Litext and
+LitextAnimation 3.6.5, SwiftMath 1.7.3, LRUCache 1.3.0, swift-cmark 0.9.0
+and swift-collections 1.7.3 — every one of them already pinned in
+`Apelin.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/Package.resolved`
+for other targets, so vendoring adds no pin.
+
+## When upstream matters
+
+This copy does not track upstream. A MarkdownView release that changes the
+renderer has to be merged into `Sources/` by hand — `git diff` against the
+tag is the whole patch. `Licenses/MarkdownView` carries the notice the
+Licenses screen shows, and `Licenses/review.json` the reviewed text hash.
